Subject: Use portable C paths instead of inline assembly and drop .debug_gdb_scripts under Fil-C
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: Take Zend's portable C paths for zend_string_equal_val, zend_safe_address, and overflow arithmetic (avoiding asm goto callbr), guard x87 inline asm to __i386__, spell xgetbv directly instead of raw .byte opcodes, and omit the raw inline-asm .debug_gdb_scripts section under __FILC__.
Upstream-Status: Upstream-Candidate
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: fd1f26a649078e4e12cb01026cf43199b6e6d160 95f267d64fd1615bae8c6c25425d9b7857bee326
Origin-Kind: filc-upstream
Origin-Project: pizlonator/fil-c
Origin-Commit: fd1f26a649078e4e12cb01026cf43199b6e6d160
Origin-URL: https://github.com/pizlonator/fil-c/commit/fd1f26a649078e4e12cb01026cf43199b6e6d160

diff --git a/Zend/zend_cpuinfo.c b/Zend/zend_cpuinfo.c
index 45857a7..9f81758 100644
--- a/Zend/zend_cpuinfo.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_cpuinfo.c
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ static unsigned get_xcr0_eax(void) {
 	// directly because older assemblers do not include support for xgetbv and
 	// there is no easy way to conditionally compile based on the assembler used.
 	unsigned eax, edx;
-	__asm__(".byte 0x0f, 0x01, 0xd0" : "=a"(eax), "=d"(edx) : "c"(0));
+	__asm__("xgetbv" : "=a"(eax), "=d"(edx) : "c"(0));
 	return eax;
 # elif defined(ZEND_WIN32) && defined(_XCR_XFEATURE_ENABLED_MASK)
 	return _xgetbv(_XCR_XFEATURE_ENABLED_MASK);
